### api/discovery -- public search, tag pages, browse and the tag cloud (M6 PRs a, b)
#
# No token needed: results are published projects of public profiles and public
# profiles, the same for everyone (a private or draft project never appears, the
# owner included). A token that is sent is verified and only changes whose rate
# budget is used.
#
# Behind the frontend, an anonymous visitor's address is forwarded with
#   X-Client-IP: <address>
#   X-Gradfolio-Proxy-Secret: <the shared secret>
# Without a valid secret the header is ignored.

@baseUrl = {{$dotenv baseUrl}}
@accessToken = {{$dotenv accessToken}}

###
# @name search
# 200 { query, people: { items, hasMore }, projects: { items, hasMore } }: the best few of each.
# Short words (AI, ML, Go, C#) match whole skills/technologies/tags and word starts; "the"/"an"
# are ignored beside other words. q is 1 to 100 characters, at most 6 words; more is 400.
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/search?q=ML

###
# @name searchShortWord
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/search?q=C%23

###
# @name searchArmenian
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/search?q=%D4%B1%D6%80%D5%B4%D5%A5%D5%B6

###
# @name searchPeople
# 200 { items: PersonSummary[], nextCursor }. Pass nextCursor back as cursor; another list's cursor is 400.
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/search/people?q=designer&limit=12

###
# @name searchProjects
# 200 { items: ProjectCard[], nextCursor }.
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/search/projects?q=iot&limit=12

###
# @name searchSignedIn
# The same results; the token only picks the rate budget.
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/search?q=iot
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

###
# @name searchEmpty
# 400 VALIDATION_FAILED: q is required and must not be blank.
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/search?q=%20

###
# @name searchTooLong
# 400 VALIDATION_FAILED: at most 100 characters and 6 words.
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/search?q=a%20b%20c%20d%20e%20f%20g

###
# @name tag
# 200 { name, projectCount, peopleCount }; name is the site-wide spelling. 404 NOT_FOUND when no public
# project or profile uses it (also for a name used only privately). A query parameter, so C# and CI/CD
# need no escaping beyond URL encoding.
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/tags?name=react

###
# @name tagProjects
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/tags/projects?name=C%23&limit=12

###
# @name tagPeople
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/tags/people?name=ml&limit=12

###
# @name tagCloud
# 200 { items: [{ name, projects, people }], generatedAt }, most used first. Served from a one-minute
# cache: a change can take that long to show. limit at most 100 (400 above).
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/tags/cloud?limit=40

###
# @name browseProjects
# 200 { items: ProjectCard[], nextCursor }: published projects of public profiles, newest first.
# sort=newest (default) or updated; optional category and status. Pass nextCursor back as cursor.
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/projects?sort=newest&limit=12

###
# @name browseProjectsByCategory
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/projects?sort=updated&category=research&status=completed

###
# @name browseUsers
# 200 { items: PersonSummary[], nextCursor }: public people, newest sign-up first (sort=newest is
# the only order and may be sent). school, major and gradYear filter on one education entry that
# must match all of them; take the choices from /v1/users/facets.
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/users?sort=newest&limit=6

###
# @name browseUsersFiltered
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/users?school=NPUA&gradYear=2026

###
# @name userFacets
# 200 { schools, majors, years: [{ value, count }], generatedAt }, most common first, at most 50 each.
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/users/facets

###
# @name browseBadSort
# 400 VALIDATION_FAILED: sort is newest or updated here (users: newest only).
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/projects?sort=oldest
